<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to sell 30,000/T March fuel oil.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to sell 30,000/T March fuel oil.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to sell 30,000 tonnes of 3.0-percent sulphur fuel oil for loading in March, a company official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The high sulphur cargo is for March 12-28 lifting, free-on-board basis from Kaohsiung, the official said.</p>
<p>The tender closes on February 24 and offers are valid for two days.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3571)</p>
